;;; A bare `_` as an activator's argument is dropped at load, in silence —
;;; regression `activator-arg` (`corpus/regressions.toml`),
;;; under Q-M1e2.22.
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A rule `q` with one parameter, and its activator `(q _)`, which writes the
;;; bare `_` as the parameter's value.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A bare `_` is reserved and names nothing (Q-M1e2.22), so the program is
;;; refused at load, with a line naming the place: every command that reads it
;;; exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered, and what it answers ──────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `ec004a48` (the engine `916d97ac`'s), release and debug alike: the
;;; loader dropped the `_` and stored the activator `(q)`, which binds no
;;; parameter, so `q` never fired, with no line. Root held no `hit`, H was
;;; `{(hit a)}` and R two states, exit 0 (`ein solve FILE`, `ein oracle
;;; FILE`). Today the parse refuses the `_`: *unexpected `_`: _ (reserved)*.

(relation p T) (relation hit T)
(p a)
(rule q (?x) :match (p ?x) :assert (hit ?x))
(q _)
